\ lib/streams.1z - Stream constructors layered on the native primitives.

\\ Bidirectional stream over stdin (read) and stdout (write).
\\ The stdin/stdout fd-close guard makes stream-close a no-op against the
\\ standard descriptors, so the value can be constructed and closed freely
\\ without affecting the process's stdio. Primary consumer is cgi.1z, where a
\\ net/http-shaped handler ( stream R -- ) runs unchanged against the CGI
\\ transport.
<stdio-stream>: ( -- stream ) [ 0 1 <duplex-stream> ] ;
